### Backend: Stock Search API

#### [MODIFY] [stocks.py](file:///c:/Stock%20AI%20tool/backend/app/routers/stocks.py)

Add a new endpoint for searching ALL stocks (not just Nifty 500) for the custom portfolio picker:

```python
@router.get("/search-all")
async def search_all_stocks(
    q: str = Query(..., min_length=1),
    limit: int = Query(20, ge=1, le=50),
    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_db),
):
    """Search across ALL stocks in the database (not just Nifty 500).
    Returns results with a flag indicating whether we have historical data."""
    search_term = f"%{q}%"
    query = (
        select(Stock)
        .where((Stock.symbol.ilike(search_term)) | (Stock.name.ilike(search_term)))
        .limit(limit)
    )
    result = await db.execute(query)
    stocks = result.scalars().all()
    
    # Check which stocks have price data
    output = []
    for s in stocks:
        has_data = s.symbol in price_cache  # or quick DB check
        output.append({
            "symbol": s.symbol,
            "name": s.name,
            "sector": s.sector,
            "market_cap_cr": s.market_cap_cr,
            "is_nifty500": s.is_nifty500,
            "has_price_data": has_data,
        })
    return output
```

> [!NOTE]
> For stocks NOT in Nifty 500, we'll show a subtle warning badge in the UI: *"Limited data — backtest may not be available"*. This keeps things honest without blocking the user.

